!
! A proposed dose within the plan's declared limits, as a number to count
! with (poultice_rules.h PR3), in Trebago, one dose per row: 1 when every
! margin (dosegap, daygap, waitgap: the limit less the proposal) is 0 or
! more, else 0. For integers min(1, max(0, a + 1)) is 1 exactly when
! a >= 0. Trebago holds dosegap and waitgap to -999999999 .. 999999999 and
! daygap to -999 .. 99: outside, ok is 0 and the answer a division by
! zero, refused, where dose_n.kron answers: held. Advice only: the
! clinician sets the limits, a carer acts.
trebago dosen
  in  dosegap(n), daygap(n), waitgap(n)
  out within(n)
  var ok(n)
  ok(i) = min(1, max(0, dosegap(i) + 1000000000)) * min(1, max(0, 1000000000 - dosegap(i))) &
        * min(1, max(0, daygap(i) + 1000)) * min(1, max(0, 100 - daygap(i))) &
        * min(1, max(0, waitgap(i) + 1000000000)) * min(1, max(0, 1000000000 - waitgap(i)))
  within(i) = min(1, max(0, dosegap(i) + 1)) * min(1, max(0, daygap(i) + 1)) &
            * min(1, max(0, waitgap(i) + 1)) / ok(i)
end
